# 02-blit-runs: blitRd (every sprite, card picture and background structure) without a call per run of pixels.
#
# The game's blitRd reads the run-length bytes through Rd::next() (its fields live in memory, so each byte is several
# loads and stores) and draws each run with a call: gfx_hline for runs over 2 pixels, pset for each pixel of shorter
# ones. On the GBA, blitRd, gfx_hline and pset were ~13 ms of a GAME OVER frame. This patch renames the game's to
# old_blitRd (kept, out of IWRAM, for the GBA_SCENECHECK build; otherwise unused and dropped) and includes
# blit_runs.inc, a blitRd that keeps the reader in registers and writes the runs itself, with the same clipping:
# gfx_hline's (the library's clip rectangle) for long runs, pset's (the screen) for short ones.

